(
K17 truss2/truss3 (2026-10-06): the geometric (initial-force) stiffness
N/L (I - n n) of the nonlinear truss memories lets a -updated truss
under a transverse load rotate to the load. Professional test
other/truss2: unit truss along x, EA = 1, node 2 loaded with (0.1, 0.1)
in one step of 0.1 (force ramp 1 at t = 1), 100 iterations. The truss
aligns with the load: reactions (0.1, 0.1) at node 1, N = 0.141421, node
2 veli (-0.176422, 0.823578) (Professional -0.176420, 0.823577). GNU
before K17: no transverse stiffness, "iterative solver broke down",
reaction velx -0.99997, rc 1.
)
echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 2
materi_velocity
materi_velocity_integrated
end_initia
mesh -follow_material -follow_material
node 1  0 0
node 2  1 0
element 1  -truss 1 2
group_type 0  -truss
group_truss_memory 0  -updated
group_truss_area 0  1.0
group_truss_elasti_young 0  1.0
bounda_dof 0  1 -velx -vely
bounda_time    0  0. 0. 1. 0.
bounda_force   1  2 -velx -vely
bounda_time    1  0. 0. 1. 1.
control_timestep                   0  1.e-1 1.e-1
control_timestep_iterations        0  100
target_item    0  -node_rhside 1 -velx
target_value   0  1.e-1 1.e-4
target_item    1  -node_rhside 1 -vely
target_value   1  1.e-1 1.e-4
target_item    2  -element_truss_force 1 0
target_value   2  0.141421 1.e-5
target_item    3  -node_dof 2 -veliy
target_value   3  0.82358 1.e-4
end_data
